preConditionHook:
// Brooks's discipline rule: "look for only three to five reasonable trades a
// day". Once the session's trade count reaches the cap, no further entries
// are taken until the next session. Book value three to five; default 5.
//
// COUNTING. A trade is counted when the position CHANGES to a non-flat state:
// mp != 0 and mp != prevMp. That counts flat->long, flat->short AND a
// REVERSAL, which opens a new position without ever passing through flat --
// the same hazard MaxPositionProfit exists for. Counting closed trades with
// TotalTrades would have been cheaper but ticks on the EXIT's fill bar, which
// is not when a trade is "taken".
//
// prevMp mirrors the twin's mp[1]: the EL variable's own one-bar history,
// zero before the strategy's first evaluated bar, which is exactly what the
// zero-initialized local gives. It is advanced in endOfFileHook so the value
// read here is always the previous bar's, as in MonthlyProfitTarget.
//
// ENTRIES ONLY, NOT FLAT. A Switch ANDs NOT(condition) into the entries AND
// ORs the condition into the exits. Brooks means only the first -- reaching
// the cap should not liquidate the trade you are in. The MarketPosition == 0
// term buys that: while a position is open the condition is false, so nothing
// is ORed into the exits, and when flat the generated exit is already guarded
// on MarketPosition at signal time and can never fire. So this Switch blocks
// entries and never forces flat, unlike MonthlyProfitTarget.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)). Direction-agnostic,
// so both sides are identical text. Intraday bars only.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    tradesToday = 0;
}
mp = ctx.MarketPosition();
if (mp != 0 && mp != prevMp) {
    tradesToday = tradesToday + 1;
}
